Experiment No.: 14

Title

Interfacing Infrared and Ultrasonic Sensors with Arduino

Aim

To interface IR and ultrasonic sensors with Arduino.

Theory

IR sensors detect objects using infrared light, while ultrasonic sensors measure distance using sound waves.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
IR Sensor
HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor
Jumper Wires
Procedure
Connect ultrasonic sensor trigger and echo pins.
Connect IR sensor output pin.
Upload the program.
Place objects near the sensors.
Observe readings.
Code
#define trigPin 9
#define echoPin 10
#define irPin 2

void setup()
{
  pinMode(trigPin,OUTPUT);
  pinMode(echoPin,INPUT);
  pinMode(irPin,INPUT);

  Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop()
{
  digitalWrite(trigPin,LOW);
  delayMicroseconds(2);

  digitalWrite(trigPin,HIGH);
  delayMicroseconds(10);

  digitalWrite(trigPin,LOW);

  long duration = pulseIn(echoPin,HIGH);

  int distance = duration*0.034/2;

  Serial.print("Distance: ");
  Serial.println(distance);

  Serial.print("IR: ");
  Serial.println(digitalRead(irPin));

  delay(500);
}
Output

Serial Monitor displays distance and IR sensor status.

Result

IR and ultrasonic sensors were successfully interfaced.

Conclusion

Object detection and distance measurement using sensors were studied.
